// A STATEMENT LET REACHED AS A VALUE REFUSES AT THE DOOR-HOLDER RATHER THAN LOWERING.
//
// THE SUBJECT IS THE NATIVE LANE'S NORMALIZE, as in
// v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position and
// v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return.
//
// v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold reads a STATEMENT let in exactly one place: body_lower_stmt_spine,
// which binds the let's key to its lowered value and the lowered REST of the spine as its body, and
// body_lower_let_expr is the door-holder for the `in` form the grammar dropped — every arm of it
// refuses, and its Present arm answers body_lowering_reason_let_body_not_reachable_from_node. So a
// let-shaped node that reaches the term dispatcher (body_lower_fold_dispatch, whose let arm calls that
// door-holder) cannot lower, whatever the source said.
//
// Two positions in the corpus hand a statement let to the VALUE reader, and both sit in the whole-corpus
// census on plain main, each keeping its file on the wave's fallback:
//
//   dag/gunbc/instruments/fabric_control_plane_live_probe.dag:1053 — the LAST statement of
//     fci1_canonical_cleanup_disposition's body is a statement let (`let disposition = match ...`, with
//     no following expression). A spine with no following statement leaves body_lower_stmt_spine through
//     its Absent arm to body_lower_tail_statement_read, which reads the statement as a VALUE: the let
//     reaches the dispatcher and refuses.
//   dag/gunbc/instruments/compute_run_unit_cold.dag:97 — the braced arm block of
//     path_is_under_production_instance_root's `ProdRoleRealizedBy { holder }` arm begins with a
//     statement let (`let root = holder.instance.instance_root`) and ends with the arm's value
//     expression, which READS that binding. The arm's body reaches the same value reader and refuses at
//     the let, before its rest is ever read.
//
// THE REDS are the two positions and their siblings, each varying one thing; THE CONTROLS are the same
// shapes that the spine already owns — a body-top-level let with a following statement, a braced arm with
// one expression, a let in an if-branch — and must resolve. The `_und` fixtures put an undeclared name in
// the position the lowering must not skip: a tail let's VALUE and an arm block's REST must both be read,
// and refuse unbound at their own atoms; and the arm-block let's binder must stay readable from its rest,
// which is what the plain `is_accepted` claim for that shape checks. A fix that dropped the binding, or
// dropped either half, would flip one of these four.
